WHAT THIS COVERS
----------------

Everything in this repository. The process itself and all of the material
that expresses it, including:

  - the delivery process: the twelve phases, sixty-nine guided tasks, the
    sequencing, the exit criteria and the definitions of done
  - all seventy-two document templates and their wording
  - the five client forms and every question in them
  - all HTML, CSS and JavaScript, including the application, the store,
    the sign-in gate, guest mode and the client portal
  - the Supabase schema and security policies
  - all written copy, documentation and setup guides
  - the SJ Development name, logo, icons and visual design

This material may not be copied, reproduced, republished, redistributed,
sublicensed, sold, rented, offered as a service, or used to create
derivative works, in whole or in part, without my written permission.

It may not be used commercially. That includes selling it, packaging it
into a product, offering it to your own clients as your own, or charging
anyone for access to it.

You are welcome to read the source, open it in your browser's developer
tools, run it locally, and learn from how it is built. That is what the
web is for, and it is why this repository is public. Lifting it wholesale,
or reusing it for your own commercial work, is a different thing.


